{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -ni \\\"protocol document|serialized document|serialize(d)? .*document|document codec|codec round-trip|round-trip\\\" ../.. -g '*.ts' -g '*.md' | head -240; rg -n \\\"CacheEntry\\\" ../../examples ../../docs -g '*.ts' -g '*.md'\"","aggregated_output":"../../packages/codemod/src/runner.ts:184:        // that followed it (also part of the same dropped trivia) so the original spacing round-trips —\n../../packages/codemod/README.md:75:protocol revision (`createMcpHandler`, multi-round-trip requests, `versionNegotiation`)\n../../docs/servers/input-required.md:223:`requestState` round-trips through the client and comes back as attacker-controlled input; the SDK applies no protection of its own. `createRequestStateCodec` returns an HMAC-SHA256 `{ mint, verify }` pair — pass `verify` as `ServerOptions.requestState.verify` and it runs before every handler entry that carries state.\n../../docs/servers/elicitation.md:66:Call `collect-feedback` and the elicitation round-trips through that handler inside the one tool call.\n../../docs/migration/upgrade-to-v2.md:474:[multi-round-trip `input_required` pattern](./support-2026-07-28.md#multi-round-trip-requests)\n../../docs/migration/upgrade-to-v2.md:996:| `InputRequiredRoundsExceeded`         | Multi-round-trip auto-fulfilment hit `maxRounds`                           |\n../../docs/migration/upgrade-to-v2.md:1250:**Round-trip the stored object verbatim and you're protected** — single-slot storage\n../../docs/migration/upgrade-to-v2.md:1287:- **Round-trip the `issuer` stamp** on persisted credentials (SEP-2352). Persist the\n../../docs/migration/upgrade-to-v2.md:1755:### `Client.connect(transport, { prior })` — zero-round-trip connect\n../../docs/migration/upgrade-to-v2.md:1763:`createMcpHandler`, `serveStdio`, `versionNegotiation`, multi-round-trip requests\n../../packages/core-internal/src/errors/sdkErrors.ts:40:     * The multi