   // Zero-round-trip reconnect from a previously-obtained\n../../packages/client/src/client/client.ts:1190:     * zero-round-trip; throws `EraNegotiationFailed` when there is no\n../../packages/client/src/client/client.ts:2259:        // any engine error) is surfaced here, per-tool, without a wasted network round-trip and\n../../test/conformance/src/everythingClient.ts:279:// multi-round-trip mock, so use the same withLocalDiscoverResponse fetch shim\n../../test/conformance/src/everythingClient.ts:336:// Multi-round-trip client scenario (SEP-2322, protocol revision 2026-07-28)\n../../test/conformance/src/everythingClient.ts:340: * The multi-round-trip client scenario's mock server only implements\n../../test/conformance/src/everythingClient.ts:416:    // multi-round-trip flows above.\n../../packages/core-internal/test/shared/inputRequired.test.ts:2: * The multi-round-trip authoring helpers (M4.1): the `inputRequired()`\n../../packages/client/src/index.ts:103:// Multi-round-trip requests (protocol revision 2026-07-28): the client-side\n../../packages/core-internal/test/shared/rawResultTypeFirst.test.ts:13: *    local error until the multi-round-trip driver (M4.1) consumes it.\n../../packages/core-internal/test/shared/inputRequiredEngine.test.ts:2: * The multi-round-trip auto-fulfilment engine wiring (the layer between the\n../../packages/core-internal/test/shared/mcpParamHeaders.test.ts:57:    test('CRLF header-injection: encode produces a sentinel value with no CR/LF and round-trips intact', () => {\n../../packages/core-internal/src/types/guards.ts:95: * 2026-07-28): the multi-round-trip return shape discriminated by\n../../packages/core-internal/test/shared/clientCapabilityRequirements.test.ts:7: * round-trip requests, and the legacy-session pre-check; the per-method\n../../packages/client/CHANGELOG.md:79:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Hide wire-only protocol members from the public surface, at the type level and at runtime. `resultType` (the 2026-07-28 result discrimination field) is no longer declared on any public result type — the wire schemas keep parsing it, and the client funnel now consumes it raw-first: `'complete'` results are stripped to the public shape and any other kind (e.g. `input_required`) rejects with the new `SdkErrorCode.UnsupportedResultType` instead of masking into an empty success. The reserved `_meta` envelope keys are lifted out of inbound requests and notifications before handlers run, and the multi-round-trip retry fields (`inputResponses`, `requestState`) out of inbound requests only (the spec reserves those names on client-initiated requests; notification params keep them), so handler params keep the 2025-era shape; for requests the lifted material surfaces at `ctx.mcpReq.envelope`, `ctx.mcpReq.inputResponses`, and `ctx.mcpReq.requestState` (notifications have no ctx — their lifted envelope keys are not surfaced). High-level client/server methods now return the named public result types (`Promise<CallToolResult>` etc.). Task wire vocabulary stays importable but is `@deprecated` and excluded from the typed method maps (`RequestMethod`/`RequestTypeMap`/`ResultTypeMap`/`NotificationTypeMap`), and `callTool` is typed as plain `CallToolResult`. See docs/migration/support-2026-07-28.md \"Wire-only members hidden from public types\".\n../../packages/client/CHANGELOG.md:85:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Add `connect(transport, { prior: DiscoverResult })` for zero-round-trip reconnect (the gateway / distributed-client pattern). Supplying a previously-obtained `DiscoverResult` skips the `server/discover` probe: on a 2026-era server `connect()` sends nothing on the wire and `callTool()` etc. work immediately. Pair with the new `client.getDiscoverResult()` (populated by the `'auto'`-mode probe, by `client.discover()`, and by `connect({ prior })` itself) — the value round-trips through `JSON.stringify`, so a gateway can probe once, persist the blob, and feed it to every worker. Only reuse a persisted `DiscoverResult` across clients that present the same authorization context as the client that obtained it.\n../../packages/client/CHANGELOG.md:100:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Per-authorization-server credential isolation (SEP-2352). `auth()` now stamps an `issuer` field onto every value it passes to `saveTokens()` / `saveClientInformation()` and threads `{ issuer }` to `tokens()` / `clientInformation()`; on read, a stored credential whose stamp names a different authorization server is treated as `undefined`, so a `client_id` / `refresh_token` issued by one AS is never sent to another. Providers that round-trip stored values verbatim are protected with no code change; multi-AS providers may key storage on `ctx.issuer`. New `AuthorizationServerMismatchError` (callback-leg gate). `OAuthClientProvider.saveAuthorizationServerUrl()` / `authorizationServerUrl()` are deprecated (still written, never read). `ClientCredentialsProvider`, `PrivateKeyJwtProvider`, `StaticPrivateKeyJwtProvider`, and `CrossAppAccessProvider` gain `expectedIssuer` and no longer define `saveClientInformation()`.\n../../packages/client/CHANGELOG.md:121:- [#2286](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/2286) [`1823aae`](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/commit/1823aae891837ebb5e3db885ec635f9efefd5771) Thanks [@felixweinberger](https://github.com/felixweinberger)! - Add the client side of multi round-trip requests (protocol revision 2026-07-28, SEP-2322). The neutral `InputRequest`/`InputResponse`/`InputRequests`/`InputResponses`/`InputRequiredResult` types and the `isInputRequiredResult()` guard ship as the neutral surface (the\n../../packages/core-internal/test/shared/protocol.test.ts:1042:        // The connection stays serviceable: the next request round-trips.\n../../packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:573:/* Multi round-trip requests (protocol revision 2026-07-28)\n../../packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:577: * request, a handler for one of the multi-round-trip methods (`tools/call`,\n../../packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:617: * The input-required result a handler for a multi-round-trip method\n../../packages/core-internal/src/types/types.ts:705: * `ResultTypeMap` except that the multi-round-trip methods (`tools/call`,\n../../test/e2e/helpers/wire-sniffer.ts:33:     * the wiring for the modern-era (2026-07-28) arms — multi-round-trip\n../../test/e2e/helpers/wire-sniffer.ts:103:        // Multi-round-trip results (protocol revision 2026-07-28) are valid\n../../test/e2e/helpers/wire-sniffer.ts:110:            fail(party, `input_required result on a cell not opted into multi-round-trip`, msg);\n../../packages/core-internal/test/shared/wireOnlyLift.test.ts:6: * `io.modelcontextprotocol/*` envelope `_meta` keys and the multi-round-trip\n../../packages/core-internal/test/corpus/specCorpus.test.ts:81:    // part of the multi-round-trip in-band vocabulary.)\n../../packages/core-internal/test/wire/encodeContract.test.ts:7: *           result vocabulary goes beyond `'complete'` (the multi round-trip\n../../packages/core-internal/test/wire/encodeContract.test.ts:80:    test('the extended-vocabulary method set is exactly the multi round-trip request methods', () => {\n../../packages/core-internal/test/wire/encodeContract.test.ts:191:    test('an input_required result from a multi round-trip method is passed through unfilled', () => {\n../../packages/core-internal/test/wire/encodeContract.test.ts:200:    test('a stray input_required from a non-multi-round-trip handler throws out of encodeResult (answered as an internal error upstream)', () => {\n../../packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:516: * @category Multi Round-Trip\n../../packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:530: * @category Multi Round-Trip\n../../packages/core-internal/src/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:547: * @category Multi Round-Trip\n../../test/integration/test/client/discoverRoundtrip.test.ts:2: * Discover round-trip: a pin-mode 2026 client completes `server/discover` →\n../../test/integration/test/client/discoverRoundtrip.test.ts:36:describe('server/discover round-trip against a modern server', () => {\n../../test/integration/test/client/discoverRoundtrip.test.ts:149:        // round-trip over HTTP completes once every modern request carries the\n../../packages/core-internal/test/shared/inputRequiredFunnel.test.ts:2: * Protocol-layer seams of the multi-round-trip flow (M4.1):\n../../packages/core-internal/test/shared/inputRequiredDriver.test.ts:2: * The multi-round-trip auto-fulfilment driver loop in isolation (M4.1):\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/hosting-entry-http.test.ts:131:    // spec's default version, so a 2025-era tools/list still round-trips.\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/tools.test.ts:890:    // Two distinct dialects must round-trip verbatim — guards against the\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/tools.test.ts:915:    // Three explicit values must round-trip verbatim — guards against the\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/jsonschema.test.ts:12: * object/Record shapes for byte-identity — round-trips them on every arm). The\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/client-auth.test.ts:2695:/** Single-slot blob provider — round-trips the SDK-stamped values verbatim. */\n../../packages/core-internal/test/types/discoverWiring.test.ts:44:    test('a discover result round-trips the schema with its advertisement intact', () => {\n../../packages/client/test/client/responseCache.test.ts:34:    it('get/set/evict/clear round-trip; evict is method-scoped; set returns the store-generated stamp', () => {\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/raw-result-type.test.ts:13: *    error (the multi-round-trip driver consumes it when it lands); an\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/raw-result-type.test.ts:134:    // multi-round-trip driver has its own requirements (typescript:mrtr:*). ----\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/protocol.test.ts:1191:    // Both requests round-tripped after the notifications, so a (non-conformant) reply to either notification would have arrived by now.\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/protocol.test.ts:1368:    // A later round-trip on the same channel proves a (non-conformant) response to the cancelled request would have arrived by now.\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/protocol.test.ts:1670:        // A post-handshake request round-trips through the consumer transport's send().\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/stdio.test.ts:118:    // framing itself is observable, not just the content round-trip.\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/stdio.test.ts:141:        // Round-trip sanity check: the multi-line payload survives intact.\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/mrtr.test.ts:2: * Multi round-trip requests (SEP-2322, protocol revision 2026-07-28) through\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/mrtr.test.ts:197:// 2026-era siblings of the push-style sampling/elicitation/roots round-trips:\n../../packages/client/test/client/inputRequiredEngine.test.ts:2: * The client-side multi-round-trip engine end to end against a scripted\n../../test/e2e/scenarios/stdio-dual-era.test.ts:58:    // pins the connection to a 2026-era instance, and tools/call round-trips\n../../test/e2e/requirements.ts:178:            'connect(transport, { prior: DiscoverResult }) against a 2026-07-28 server is zero-round-trip: a fresh client supplied with a previously-obtained DiscoverResult connects without putting any HTTP exchange on the wire, adopts the modern era directly, and callTool round-trips immediately. prior is modern-only — no modern overlap throws SdkError(EraNegotiationFailed) (no legacy fallback).',\n../../test/e2e/requirements.ts:181:        note: 'Runs on the entryModern arm; the wired (negotiating) client is the bootstrap that obtains the DiscoverResult, then a fresh worker client connects to the same harness-hosted endpoint via wired.url + a fresh StreamableHTTPClientTransport over wired.fetch with { prior }. The zero-round-trip clause is asserted on the arm-recorded httpLog length.'\n../../test/e2e/requirements.ts:463:                note: 'The 2026-07-28 wire deletes tools[].execution (taskSupport), which this body asserts round-trips.'\n../../test/e2e/requirements.ts:473:            'tools/list supports cursor pagination: the nextCursor returned by a list handler round-trips back to the handler as an opaque cursor until the listing is exhausted.'\n../../test/e2e/requirements.ts:532:        note: 'Restricted to the entryModern arm because the 2025-era wire codec keeps outputSchema/structuredContent at their type:\"object\" / Record shapes (byte-identity), so a non-object root only round-trips natively on the 2026-07-28 path.'\n../../test/e2e/requirements.ts:540:        note: 'Restricted to the entryModern arm because the array-typed outputSchema/structuredContent only round-trip natively on the 2026-07-28 wire codec.'\n../../test/e2e/requirements.ts:548:        note: 'Restricted to the entryModern arm so the schema (carrying prefixItems) round-trips through the 2026-07-28 wire codec verbatim.'\n../../test/e2e/requirements.ts:556:        note: 'Restricted to the entryModern arm because primitive structuredContent only round-trips natively on the 2026-07-28 wire codec.'\n../../test/e2e/requirements.ts:564:        note: 'Runs on the entryModern arm so the array structuredContent round-trips natively.'\n../../test/e2e/requirements.ts:571:            'A